WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.647
Can a bill become law if

2
00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:03.218
the Rajya Sabha rejects it?

3
00:00:03.539 --> 00:00:05.156
For an ordinary bill, yes.

4
00:00:05.651 --> 00:00:07.397
A bill must pass both Houses,

5
00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.435
then get the President's assent.

6
00:00:09.727 --> 00:00:10.977
If one House rejects it,

7
00:00:11.506 --> 00:00:12.760
if they finally disagree

8
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.492
on amendments,

9
00:00:13.854 --> 00:00:15.381
or if six months pass,

10
00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:16.987
the President can call a

11
00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:17.714
joint sitting.

12
00:00:18.027 --> 00:00:20.361
There, a majority of members

13
00:00:20.361 --> 00:00:22.612
of both Houses, present and

14
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:23.946
voting, decides.

15
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.846
It never applies to a Money Bill,

16
00:00:26.142 --> 00:00:27.896
and constitutional amendments

17
00:00:27.896 --> 00:00:28.863
can't go to one.

18
00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:31.616
It has happened only three times:

19
00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:36.390
in 1961, 1978 and 2002.

20
00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:37.580
Two Houses.

21
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.648
One way out of a deadlock.

22
00:00:40.319 --> 00:00:40.977
Your turn.

23
00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:42.589
Which bill can never go to

24
00:00:42.589 --> 00:00:43.401
a joint sitting?
